-- title:
--   Residue count times normalised absolute value equals one
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field (a field of characteristic zero, finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, with ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$), and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, i.e. a finite place of $K$. Write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion of $K$ with its normalised multiplicative absolute value $\|\cdot\|$, and $\mathcal{O}_v \subseteq K_v$ for the ring of $v$-adic integers. The assertion is that for every $a \in \mathcal{O}_v$ with $a \neq 0$, the quotient ring $\mathcal{O}_v / (a)$ by the ideal generated by the singleton $\{a\}$ has cardinality (as a natural number, via `Nat.card`, which is $0$ for an infinite type) whose image in $\mathbb{R}$ satisfies $$\#\bigl(\mathcal{O}_v/a\mathcal{O}_v\bigr)\cdot \|a\| = 1,$$ the norm being that of the image of $a$ in $K_v$. In particular the quotient is finite, and its cardinality is exactly $\|a\|^{-1} = q_v^{\,v(a)}$, where $q_v$ is the cardinality of the residue field at $v$.
--
--   This is the standard local index formula at a finite place: the module index of a principal ideal of the valuation ring computes the normalised absolute value of a generator, which is what makes the normalised absolute values on $K_v$ the right local factors for the product formula and for measure-theoretic computations on adeles. It is used for the determinant index formula for full-rank submodules over $\mathcal{O}_v$ and, through that, in the norm computations for determinants and traces arising in the construction of automorphic forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_natCard_adicCompletionIntegers_quotient_span_singleton_mul_norm_eq_one.lean

